WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.120
The city.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.820
A place where people gather, are born and raised, and one day pass on.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:14.040
But sometimes through the carelessness of the gods,

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.070
the lives of the city's residents can be thrown into chaos.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.500
Hotori! Dinner's ready!

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:31.510
Hotori! Did you hear me?

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:15.800
Hmm, so this is the café you work at?

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.200
Shouldn't you be at ping pong practice right now?

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.320
I'm ditching it. Can I order now?

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:21.570
Sure, what’cha want?

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:24.200
Cutlet curry, hold the cutlets.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:26.420
And an iced coffee, hold the ice. And make it hot.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:27.200
Come again?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:29.120
So you just want curry and coffee, right?

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.710
I wasn't talking to you, dumbass.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.840
So very sorry. I just work here too, that's all.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:39.090
Hey, what's going on here? It's kinda tense in here.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.540
She was an upperclassman at my middle school.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.630
She's all pissy because I didn't join the ping-pong club in high school.

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.230
She gave up 'cause she couldn't beat me, so she ran away, the little wuss.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.100
I won't take you back now, even if you beg me to.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:55.230
Hey, quit fighting over such a stupid disagreement.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:58.740
Oh yeah! I've got just the thing for you two.

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:02.490
The magnifying pendant!

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.410
At first glance, it looks like an ordinary magnifying glass.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.410
But wait! The other end is actually a fountain pendant!

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.080
That's fountain PEN. No "dant".

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:15.250
It's a little heavy, but it still writes great.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.900
Two completely different instruments, combined into one amazing detective tool!

00:03:19.900 --> 00:03:22.180
So you two stop fighting and get along with each other!

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:27.740
Huh? I thought I could work this out just like Moori Motonari's "3 arrows" story.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.430
But it seems like they're not getting it.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.900
This pen looks like it was a gift.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.310
Well yeah. How many high school girls can afford a fountain pendant?

00:03:36.310 --> 00:03:38.190
My uncle gave it to me as a present when I entered high school.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.320
This is a Montblanc.

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.720
Oh, I'm sorry, but we don't serve montblancs here.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:45.780
We've got coffee jelly, though.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.830
No, not the food. Did you modify this yourself?

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.610
Sure did! I'm gonna patent this!

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:55.710
I just chopped off the end of the pen, and super glued the magnifying glass to it!

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:58.730
Well, as long as you knew what you were doing, I guess it's okay.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:00.970
But Monblanc pens are pretty fancy, you know.

00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:04.510
I think they cost tens of thousands of yen.

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:09.010
Sorry to burst your bubble Hotori,

00:04:09.340 --> 00:04:12.020
but someone's beat you to the punch.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.450
See? The pen cap has a magnifying glass on it.

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:18.360
It's pretty popular among us old folk.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:23.490
You can go home early today. Get some rest.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.360
Let's see... I think I've got something you might like.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:26.870
Found it!

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:29.870
Here. You can have this whistle, so cheer up, okay?

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:32.820
Aren't you going to change out of that?

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:36.140
Isn't your house the other way?

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:40.900
So that's the look of someone who's lost everything they used to believe in.

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.510
It's like she's been dowsed in despair.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.720
Desperately seeking a light of hope amidst the darkness.

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:55.310
Arashiyama residence...

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:56.810
Uncle!?

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.650
What impeccable timing you have.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:02.900
That? Oh, you meant the fountain pendant?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.700
Y-Yes, of course I'm using it!

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.090
I always carry it with me. I've got it with me right here.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:11.690
By the way, how much did this cost, exactly?

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:12.080
A hundred thou-

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:17.170
During summer vacation? Yes, I'd love to come visit.

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:18.670
Thank you.

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:22.030
Hey mom, phone call from the Ayatoris.

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.420
Okay, thanks. Hey, what about work?

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:31.680
It's the de-cap-itation caper!

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:35.830
Okay, think positive.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:39.440
I'll just come up with some kind of trick to distract him when I visit.

00:05:39.670 --> 00:05:42.740
A trick... mysteries have tricks...

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.820
Mysteries... I wonder when Hiroto Shimabe's new book is coming out.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:50.320
I wonder if Mystery Magazine published any updates on it...

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.080
Oh, I know!

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.160
That's it!

00:05:57.170 --> 00:05:59.030
First prize, 5 million yen!

00:05:59.030 --> 00:05:59.830
That's more than enough!

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.420
The deadline's coming up soon.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.340
But they'll publish three months from now.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:05.300
I can still make it!

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:08.300
I can buy another fountain pendant by summer!

00:06:09.250 --> 00:06:15.470
No, writing a detective story and getting the prize money is the ONLY way to get another fountain pendant!

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.480
What would I do if I actually won first prize, though?

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:25.610
I stood on the deck of the ship, watching the waves and enjoying my jell-o.

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:30.870
But little did I know that a horrifying incident was about to take place.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.130
I can see Jelly Island!

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.670
So that's Jelly Island, home of the world-famous jelly...

00:06:39.670 --> 00:06:42.750
I've heard stories of an Abominable Jellyman that lives on the island.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:44.550
I'm so scared!

00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:51.300
Welcome, friends. I am the master of Jelly Island.

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:53.810
Please, help yourselves to some jelly.

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.850
I want strawberry jelly.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.680
This person might be the Jellyman!

00:06:58.030 --> 00:06:59.600
This is some pretty good jelly, huh?

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.190
Verily. Jelly Island's jelly is quite delectable.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:05.690
What happened!?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.680
Oh no! Tatsuno-san's dead!

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.250
She's been decapitated!

00:07:11.250 --> 00:07:12.570
Who could have done such a thing?

00:07:12.710 --> 00:07:15.200
The legend of the Abominable Jellyman was true!

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:17.730
Everybody stay together!

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:19.870
The murderer might be one of us!

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.620
No, the Jellyman did it!

00:07:21.950 --> 00:07:25.000
I don't trust any of you! I'm going on alone!

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:30.380
That was Kon-senpai's scream!

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:33.760
Now Kon-senpai's been killed too!

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.770
Heh, now I know who the culprit is.

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:44.540
I thought it was strange that the body of the first victim, Tatsuno-san, disappeared without a trace.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.540
But in fact, it's just the opposite!

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.320
The murderer is YOU!

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:50.690
Kon-senpai!

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:52.460
But she's already dead!

00:07:53.550 --> 00:07:56.160
This isn't blood. It's strawberry jelly.

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:59.660
Observe. She merely buried herself!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.670
The only victim here is Tatsuno-san!

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:07.710
Dammit! She wouldn't join the ping pong club, so I killed her!

00:08:08.110 --> 00:08:10.070
All right, you're going downtown.

00:08:10.580 --> 00:08:12.970
Splendid work as always, Arashiyama-kun.

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.970
Inspector Moriaki.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:17.800
'Twas a dreadful case...

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:23.940
But perhaps Kon-senpai was also a victim of society.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:24.840
The end.

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.460
You sure seem happy today.

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:36.120
You looked like you hadn't been getting enough sleep recently.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:39.990
Oh, Kon-senpai...

00:08:40.710 --> 00:08:43.130
Arashiyama-sensei, when is your next book coming out?

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:44.790
Please give me your autograph!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.750
Me too, if you don't mind, Arashiyama-kun!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.460
Everyone line up and prepare more flattery for me.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.210
I’ll still come visit you when I'm famous.

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:53.720
Huh?

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:56.590
I'm home!

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.890
Hmm? I got something from Mystery Magazine.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.890
It's still a long time before they announce the winners...

00:09:04.430 --> 00:09:09.400
Let's see..."Thank you very much for your entry.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:17.660
However, we regret to inform you that your submission did not advance past the initial round of our rigorous evaluation."

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:28.290
<b>Submission</b>

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:30.290
<b>Initial Round</b>

00:09:31.300 --> 00:09:32.300
<b>Please do not be discouraged. Rather, we look forward to seeing you improve as a writer.</b>

00:09:36.290 --> 00:09:39.400
T-This can't be happening!

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:42.710
I spent two whole weeks writing that! It's not fair!

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:53.260
H-Hey little girl, you okay!?

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.650
Call an ambulance!

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:59.650
Sorry for jumping out in front of you like that.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:01.150
I'm fine though, don't worry.

00:10:01.150 --> 00:10:02.340
I'm calling an ambulance right now, okay?

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:04.040
Wait! Don't move the body!

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:06.160
Oh man, she's a goner...

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:11.500
Hmm, this might be a little... no, a BIG problem.

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:13.750
Hey, I can see through myself!

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:16.510
Ah! I'm floating!

00:10:16.890 --> 00:10:17.880
Hey, what gives!?

00:10:18.290 --> 00:10:20.140
This isn't funny!

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:29.650
Hey, something's coming!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:31.440
Who the heck are you guys!?

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:32.400
Go away! Shoo!

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:35.560
No really, this isn't a good time.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:37.860
I said wait! Put me back down!

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:40.740
Hey, if you're just gonna goof off, can you let it slide this time?

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:46.580
Hey! Is that supposed to be my life flashing before my eyes!?

00:10:49.030 --> 00:10:51.540
The city is home to many people.

00:10:51.990 --> 00:10:55.960
And just like that, there is now one less.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:02.510
Place thine heart upon this scale.

00:11:02.860 --> 00:11:05.690
If thine heart is of lesser weight than this plum, thou may enter heaven.

00:11:05.690 --> 00:11:06.890
Be it heavier, and thou be banished to hell.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:10.520
There's no way a heart could be lighter than a feather!

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.970
No! The holy feather!

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:16.510
Think of something better to compare it to.

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.780
Like a can of coffee or something.

00:11:19.610 --> 00:11:21.380
What are you doing here!?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.380
You're Japanese, so get in the Japanese line!

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:29.040
Come back here you little brat! I’ll throw you into hell!

00:11:31.850 --> 00:11:35.740
Arashiyama-san... Arashiyama Hotori-san...

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:39.690
Okay... Arashiyama Hotori-san, yes?

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:41.600
Is this your first time dying?

00:11:41.600 --> 00:11:42.090
Yeah.

00:11:42.660 --> 00:11:45.300
Cause of death: accident. No negative karma.

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:46.260
Okay, that will be all.

00:11:47.030 --> 00:11:51.640
There aren't any problems, so you should receive your proof of residence in about two to three weeks.

00:11:56.820 --> 00:11:59.280
This place kinda reminds me of city hall.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:01.530
Hi there, sorry about before.

00:12:01.790 --> 00:12:05.280
My job is to assist new residents, so feel free to ask me anything.

00:12:09.320 --> 00:12:11.030
Is this really the afterlife?

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:13.000
It's not exactly how I pictured it.

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:15.830
Nobody's got halos or those triangle thingies?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:20.670
We stopped doing those decades ago to cut costs.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:24.340
It's not quite the same, but you can have this.

00:12:26.030 --> 00:12:27.010
Ooh, pretty.

00:12:27.010 --> 00:12:29.560
It looks great on you. It's called a "silent flower".

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:33.330
'Cause dead men tell no tales! Get it?

00:12:34.150 --> 00:12:35.350
I've always wanted to say that.

00:12:35.570 --> 00:12:37.860
Well? Wasn't that hilarious?

00:12:39.560 --> 00:12:41.020
Are you trying to kill me?

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:43.500
Lay off, would you? I just died y'know!

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.110
How about a little consideration?

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.370
What's this place? An arcade?

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.500
The one and only place in Heaven where you can interact with the world of the living.

00:12:54.850 --> 00:12:56.820
How about we have some fun?

00:12:56.820 --> 00:12:58.770
It's on me today.

00:12:58.770 --> 00:13:01.000
So they've got photo booths in heaven too?

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:06.140
Photo booth? Honestly, you living folk...

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:09.010
Don't treat me like I'm some hick visiting the city.

00:13:11.230 --> 00:13:13.660
This is called "Spirit Photoshop".

00:13:13.660 --> 00:13:16.430
You can make ordinary Earth pictures into spirit shots.

00:13:16.430 --> 00:13:17.870
That sounds like fun!

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:20.880
If you have anyone in mind, go right ahead.

00:13:20.880 --> 00:13:21.570
How about Kon-senpai?

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.220
What's her full name?

00:13:23.220 --> 00:13:24.070
Kon Futaba.

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.820
Perfect! It just so happens she recently dropped some off to be developed.

00:13:28.570 --> 00:13:32.450
Now we buy hands, faces or poses, and place them in any photo you like.

00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:34.760
Hey, does it have bunny ears?

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:37.540
Wouldn't bunny ears make for a hilarious picture?

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:42.670
Oh, those kinds of poses are rather expensive.

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:46.720
It's a bit pricey for us common folk.

00:13:46.720 --> 00:13:47.880
Yeah, you're right.

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:50.430
Stuff like faces, fists, or will-o’-the-wisps are much cheaper.

00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:53.980
No wonder all those pictures look the same.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.910
Okay, I'll go with this hand then.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:04.470
Now that I've tweaked her picture, I wanna see Kon-senpai's reaction.

00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.740
Yes, of course.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:09.740
Okay then, you can try these next.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.790
Deposit 100 yen, and you can view the Earth for a brief time.

00:14:14.250 --> 00:14:15.750
Hey, I see it!

00:14:16.450 --> 00:14:17.630
It's a bath house.

00:14:18.430 --> 00:14:20.380
Wow, this is so cool!

00:14:21.180 --> 00:14:23.580
Huh? Mosaics?

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.350
Private places cannot be viewed.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:29.810
Oh yeah... whatever happened to my body anyway?

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:30.840
Maruko Hospital

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.100
Hey, there's mom.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:37.270
So you're saying Hotori's going to be like that permanently?

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:42.520
It breaks my heart to say this, but we don't believe she'll ever regain consciousness.

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.020
That can't be...

00:14:44.280 --> 00:14:46.390
Please, you've got to do something! Please doctor!

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:48.200
Where's dad running off to?

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:51.280
Takeru... Yukiko...

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.230
Stop crying, Yukiko.

00:14:53.230 --> 00:14:54.730
I said stop crying!

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.790
Crying's not gonna bring her back.

00:15:01.790 --> 00:15:05.130
Hey, I said stop... crying!

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.260
Why? Why did this have to happen?

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.240
What did Arashiyama-san do to deserve this?

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:23.390
It'll be okay. Hotori will get better.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.530
How do you know that for sure?

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:27.750
I just do!

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.940
Don't give me that crap!

00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:31.570
How can you say that so easily!?

00:15:31.570 --> 00:15:32.360
Because!

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:35.200
Because Hotori can't die yet! She just can't!

00:15:43.560 --> 00:15:46.020
Yes... I see...

00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:47.790
You have my condolences.

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:49.760
Thank you. Please excuse me.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:06.770
I don't care! Bring me that fucking driver's head right now!

00:16:07.150 --> 00:16:09.160
I'll run HIM over with my truck!

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:11.230
Just calm down, guys!

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:14.250
Huh!? You trying to defend him?

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:16.870
You're gonna regret it, pal!

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:19.740
Stop it, guys.

00:16:19.740 --> 00:16:23.000
Hotori-chan would resent us for that.

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:28.500
Thank you. My business here is finished.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:42.140
Zenji-san, please watch over Hotori for me. Please...

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:48.760
Sorry, Uki... there's nothing I can do.

00:16:51.290 --> 00:16:54.780
WHY!? Why did you have to die, Arashiyama!?

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:58.950
I... I never got to tell you how I feel...

00:16:59.460 --> 00:16:59.910
I still haven't told you that...

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.160
...to your face yet!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:05.580
Why is this happening!?

00:17:11.010 --> 00:17:13.960
Please, God! Give Hotori back to us!

00:17:13.960 --> 00:17:16.300
She didn't even make it past 16!

00:17:16.610 --> 00:17:19.860
Can't you do something about it!?

00:17:25.520 --> 00:17:28.230
This is the first time anyone's been this worried about me.

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.560
I'll have to be more careful next time...

00:17:31.560 --> 00:17:33.260
I'll try to be less of a klutz...

00:17:42.000 --> 00:17:46.040
Oh yeah... there won't be a "next time"...

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:52.600
Ever... again...

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:59.300
I wanted to be with them a little longer.

00:18:00.160 --> 00:18:03.810
I wanted to live a little longer!

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:12.110
You must've had a wonderful life if you feel that way.

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:16.780
There are people who end their lives of their own volition, you know.

00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:20.280
Besides, this place has its good points too.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.920
Everyone comes here eventually.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:24.540
If you just work hard and be patient, you'll see them again soon.

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:25.790
Right?

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:31.540
Yeah, you're right.

00:18:31.900 --> 00:18:38.300
I'm gonna work hard and make lots of money so I can put bunny ears in their pictures.

00:18:38.440 --> 00:18:39.760
That's the spirit!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:42.600
Well then, I'll help you find a job then.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:48.830
You're young, so how about dressing as an angel and greeting the deceased?

00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:50.580
Oh yeah, like those kids?

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:52.440
My son does it too.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.170
Arashiyama Hotori-sama.

00:18:58.890 --> 00:19:03.370
Please report at once to the Heaven Immigration Bureau.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.200
That's me...

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.210
What!? I can go back!?

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.120
Yes, that seems to be the case.

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:16.460
In your case, your body on Earth is perfectly intact, yes?

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:22.590
Your brain made a miraculous recovery, so you may return if you wish.

00:19:25.630 --> 00:19:28.100
Sorry you can't come with me, mister.

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:31.380
People return just like you every now and then.

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:33.100
You take care now and don't worry about me.

00:19:33.490 --> 00:19:36.860
When I get back, I'll go visit your grave.

00:19:37.360 --> 00:19:40.490
Sorry, but once you return, you'll lose your memory of your time here.

00:19:41.300 --> 00:19:42.300
Oh, that's too bad...

00:19:42.780 --> 00:19:44.990
Well then, hope to see you again next time!

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.990
All right, are you ready to go?

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.970
Being a guide sounds like a nice job and all,

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:09.520
but really, all I do is just help them come to grips with the reality of their deaths.

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:12.520
It's the saddest, most cruel job there is.

00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:18.780
That girl being able to return is like a special blessing to me.

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.860
Come on, let's get back to work.

00:20:35.840 --> 00:20:39.050
It feels like I just had a really weird dream.

00:20:42.090 --> 00:20:44.760
Huh!? What the heck!? Is this Candid Camera or something!?

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:49.260
Doctor, come quick! Arashiyama-san's awake!

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.490
The city.

00:20:51.490 --> 00:20:57.270
A place where people gather, are born and raised, and one day pass on.

00:20:57.910 --> 00:21:00.410
But sometimes through the carelessness of the gods,

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:03.280
the lives of the city's residents can be thrown into chaos.

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:05.030
Even so...

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.160
Hotori!

00:21:08.810 --> 00:21:10.410
Hey, Kon-senpai!

00:21:10.710 --> 00:21:12.660
I was worried sick, you idiot!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:15.670
Even so, the city turns.

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:21.620
So then, once my dad dumped 3,400 yen into the donation box, I woke up.

00:21:21.620 --> 00:21:24.990
I mean, it's like "you're worth about 3400 yen".

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:27.080
Sounds about right.

00:21:27.080 --> 00:21:30.310
Oh yeah, and about that fountain pendant...

00:21:30.570 --> 00:21:34.210
I told them it got crushed when the truck hit me.

00:21:34.210 --> 00:21:37.060
Your brain's only good for getting yourself out of trouble, huh?

00:21:40.480 --> 00:21:41.800
By the way, Hotori.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:48.700
I think this mess you caught up in was because an evil spirit possessed you.

00:21:49.110 --> 00:21:52.780
Huh? Have you gone crazy or something?

00:21:52.780 --> 00:21:54.390
Why the heck would you say that out of the blue?

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:56.710
Shut up! Just look at this.

00:21:57.150 --> 00:21:57.950
See?

00:21:57.950 --> 00:22:00.020
We took this picture together the other day, remember?

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:01.670
Look at your shoulder.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:05.980
What's that!? That's freaky!

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:10.500
And the town still turns.

00:23:37.300 --> 00:23:39.950
Thank you very maid for coming!
